            "image_1": "shopify://shop_images/SC26_4x5_Rip_Instructions_1.jpg",
            "caption_1": "Find the perforation hidden beneath the header, about 1cm / 0.5\" from the bottom.",
            "image_2": "shopify://shop_images/SC26_4x5_Rip_Instructions_2.jpg",
            "caption_2": "Hold the header steady with one hand, and start a small tear of about 1 cm / ½″ along the perforation",
            "image_3": "shopify://shop_images/SC26_4x5_Rip_Instructions_3.jpg",
            "caption_3": "Don’t tear sideways along the perforation - it won’t rip cleanly. Instead, grip the bottom of the sheet, below the rip, and pull straight down.",
            "image_4": "shopify://shop_images/SC26_4x5_Rip_Instructions_4.jpg",
            "caption_4": "Keep it taut as it separates. Detached sheets make great wrapping paper."
